===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# [[yes|Yes]], [[certainly]]; expression indicating strong agreement.
#: {{ux|en|Is Bob a good teacher?<br>'''Absolutely!'''}}
#: {{ux|en|Do you want a free cookie with that coffee?<br>'''Absolutely!'''}}

====Usage notes====
* Some commentators, especially in England, criticise the interjectional use as having no meaning beyond that of {{m|en|yes}}.<ref name="SLE-usage">{{R:She Literally Exploded|page=3}}.</ref> This is not to mean that [[emphasis]] is useless, which of course, [[pragmatics|pragmatically speaking]], it isn’t; rather, it means that ''absolutely'' is better avoided when there is no emphasis, or, in other words, when the meaning is simply ''Yes'' (compare, in French, the use of ''Tout à fait'' as an answer, with the meaning of ''Oui'', which is advised against by the Trésor de la langue française informatisé). On the other hand, emphasis can also be expressed in other ways: for instance, ''Yes, of course'', ''Yes, indeed'', ''Yes, certainly''.

